\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{The partition coefficient of a two-by-two sign torus}
\date{2026-11-19}

\p{Use the [labeled cellular torus](fdip-00SH) with both periods
two. At each of its #{4} vertices place a sign #{\phi_x}. Each of
its #{8} positive labeled links carries an independent sign #{U_e}.
Each of its #{4} square faces uses the two coordinate directions,
traversing its boundary once. The two positive links between any
neighboring pair remain distinct, as in \ref{fdip-00SM}. Give each
face weight #{2} when its product is #{+1} and weight #{1} when its
product is #{-1}. Give transported agreement factor #{2} and disagreement
factor #{1}. With unit site weights, the [joint counting
sum](fdip-010E) is #{Z=550656}.}

\p{Write #{U_f} for the sign product around face #{f}, and for
each edge put #{u_e=\phi_{h(e)}U_e\phi_{s(e)}}. A sign #{z} has
the required factor #{(3+z)/2}. Compute the integer sum over the
rationals by expanding the product of these #{12} factors.
A term selects a set #{A} of faces and a set #{B} of edges whose
signs occur, with coefficient #{2^{-12}3^{12-|A|-|B|}}. Let
#{E_A} be the labeled edges traversed an odd number of times by
the selected face boundaries. In the monomial
#{\prod_{f\in A}U_f\prod_{e\in B}u_e}, summation over each
independent #{U_e} is zero unless #{B=E_A}.}

\p{At each vertex the traversals of a closed face walk meet its
endpoints in pairs. Taking their union modulo two leaves an even
number of edge ends of #{E_A} at each vertex. Thus when #{B=E_A},
every site sign also has even exponent. The monomial is then one
on all #{2^{12}} joint configurations, canceling the denominator.
The contribution of #{A} is #{3^{12-|A|-|E_A|}}.}

\p{The empty set and the full set of faces have empty boundary.
A singleton has #{4} boundary edges, as does its complement. Of
the #{6} pairs, #{4} pairs are neighbors in the same row or column.
Each shares two labeled edges and leaves #{4} boundary edges.
The other two pairs share no edge and leave #{8}. Summing gives
##{\begin{aligned}
 Z={}&3^{12}+4\cdot3^7+4\cdot3^6\\
    &+2\cdot3^2+4\cdot3^5+3^8=550656.
\end{aligned}}}
